.TH "MAKNOON" "1" "Jan 2024" "Maknoon Post-Quantum Engine" "Maknoon Manual"

.SH NAME
maknoon-mcp - Start the Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for AI Agent integration


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaknoon mcp [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Launches the native Maknoon MCP server. This allows AI agents to interact
with the engine's cryptographic tools over standard I/O (stdio) or HTTP (sse).

.PP
For SSE mode, the server uses Go 1.23's native Post-Quantum TLS 1.3 capabilities
(ML-KEM hybrid) to ensure a quantum-resistant transport handshake.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--address\fP=":8080"
	Address to listen on for SSE mode

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for mcp

.PP
\fB--tls-cert\fP=""
	Path to TLS certificate for SSE HTTPS

.PP
\fB--tls-key\fP=""
	Path to TLS private key for SSE HTTPS

.PP
\fB--transport\fP="stdio"
	Transport mode (stdio, sse)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--fips\fP[=false]
	Enforce strict FIPS-140 compliant cryptographic standards

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output results in JSON format

.PP
\fB--passphrase-file\fP=""
	Read passphrase from a file instead of prompting (use - for stdin). Also settable via MAKNOON_PASSPHRASE_FILE

.PP
\fB--policy\fP=""
	Path to a declarative governance policy file (JSON)

.PP
\fB--tpm\fP[=false]
	Enable TPM 2.0 hardware-backed storage for keys

.PP
\fB--tpm-device\fP="/dev/tpmrm0"
	Path to the TPM device node

.PP
\fB--tpm-pcrs\fP=[]
	List of PCRs to bind keys to (e.g., 7,14)

.PP
\fB--trace\fP[=false]
	Enable low-level diagnostic tracing to stderr


